{"content":[{"c":["EN-GEDI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A vital oasis on the west side of the Dead Sea about 35 miles (56.3 kilometers) southeast of Jerusalem. Allotted to Judah’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.62","r":"Josh.15.62","rawR":"Josh.15.62","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.62","value":"Josh.15.62"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:62"},"), En-gedi contained a hot water spring coming from the side of a limestone cliff, producing semitropical vegetation. The area became known for its palms, vineyards, and balsam (",{"href":"?bref=Song.1.14","r":"Song.1.14","rawR":"Song.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.1.14","value":"Song.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 1:14"},"; Josephus’s ",{"c":["Antiquities"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," 20.1.2). The ancient site was southeast of the oasis at Tell el-Jarn near modern ’Ain Jidi."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["En-gedi was called Hazazon-tamar in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.2","r":"2Chr.20.2","rawR":"2Chr.20.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.2","value":"2Chr.20.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 20:2"},", and figured in several OT events. There Kedorlaomer conquered the Amorites (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.7","r":"Gen.14.7","rawR":"Gen.14.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.7","value":"Gen.14.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:7"},"); David sought refuge from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.23.29","r":"1Sam.23.29","rawR":"1Sam.23.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.23.29","value":"1Sam.23.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 23:29"},"); and in Ezekiel’s vision of Israel’s restoration, fishermen would catch fish from the Dead Sea from En-gedi to En-eglaim (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.10","r":"Ezek.47.10","rawR":"Ezek.47.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.10","value":"Ezek.47.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"EnGedi","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:62","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.62","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.62","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.62"},{"anchorText":"Sg 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.1.14","rawQueryValue":"Song.1.14","sourceRefExact":"Song.1.14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chronicles 20:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.2","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.2","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.7","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.7","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 23:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.23.29","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.23.29","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.23.29"},{"anchorText":"Ez 47:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.47.10","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.47.10","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.47.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cf0b0736f27c8931718b5f91649b0ea248fdbd40faa5e7d4656f0af1ed06cdcf","sourceItemName":"EnGedi","sourceItemOrder":172,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"EnGedi","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"En-Gedi","title":"En-Gedi","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}